PROPOSED — NOT FINAL. Jeff writes the licence text.

Three things are in here and they do not take the same terms.

1. CODE AND STYLESHEET (chrome.js, assets/brand.css, test/)
   Proposed: MIT. A permissive licence keeps the repository public, which is
   what lets the Lightsail box install it without credentials.

2. FONTS (assets/fonts/)
   Not GateIron's to license. Fraunces and Hanken Grotesk are under the SIL
   Open Font License 1.1, which permits bundling and redistribution provided
   the licence travels with them and they are not sold on their own. Both
   texts are in that directory and must stay there.

3. THE GATE MARK (assets/gate-*.png) AND THE NAME
   GateIron, LLC's. Publishing the files here grants no permission to use the
   mark or the name. Proposed: "The GateIron name and the gate mark are
   trademarks of GateIron, LLC. No licence to use them is granted by this
   repository."

   The mark is already downloadable from gateiron.com, so a public repository
   exposes nothing new. If it should not ship here at all, gateMark() can read
   a path from the assets option and the consumer supplies the file.
